module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a call expression is erased by v2 normalize before resolve runs, so every reference it carries -- callee and arguments -- is invisible to name resolution and the refusal a missing declaration should raise has nothing to fire on** (INVALID STATE: v2.compiler.normalize, via v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold, lowers a function body that is a call into a Transform node whose only child is the `dag_token_lbrace` atom. The callee identity and every argument subtree are dropped. The module then passes normalize and resolve Accepted, with no diagnostic of any severity).",

    "HARM. v2 name resolution fails OPEN for the whole call-expression population, declared and undeclared alike. A call to a name no declaration provides is Accepted. The namespace cut's census rests on a delete-first premise, that removing an authority makes every real dependent REFUSE LOUDLY, and that premise is void for every dependent reached through a call. For the observed call shapes, erasure prevents the missing-callee resolution refusal from firing. Consequently a refusal roster cannot establish completeness of affected call dependents from absence of refusals. The affected population has not been established by these receipts. Native census mode separately performs no resolution and therefore cannot establish binding-refusal completeness. A native run with no passing call-bearing identities does not by itself identify lowering as the cause of every refused identity.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, because two neighbouring rows look like this one and are not. `unresolved_callee_conflated_with_dispatched_elsewhere` is the v1 ExprCall-tail class: there the callee reaches the classifier and the miss is absorbed later. Here the callee never reaches resolve at all. And the earlier dated measurements (v2.test.claim.staged_front_end unbound_symbol_reason_note, v2.test.claim.dag_acceptance frontier_arm_note) attributed the silence to resolve. That was the wrong stage: resolve is correct over the tree it receives, and the tree has already lost the call. A wall authored in resolve would therefore be a decoration (DESIGN section 4b), because the undeclared-callee RED and the declared-callee positive control arrive as identical trees.",

    "RECEIPT (2026-09-12, still-eagle-447, NAMESPACE XL-2 scoping). The normalized tree was dumped for five bodies via prepare_grammar, parse_module_prepared and normalize -- the calls v2.compiler.program_assembly program_assembly_read_to_normalized_root_prepared makes, and so the census route's own hand-off (v2.compiler.compile native_test_context_from_ingest). (That composition was DELETED by gunbc#11985, which threaded one occurrence allocator across the ingest and left it with no caller; the receipt is dated and its reading stands, but the live route is now program_assembly_read_to_normalized_root_seeded.) `{ k }` keeps `Atom:k`. `{ x }` over a parameter keeps `Atom:x`. `{ g(x: 1) }` with g declared, `{ zzz(x: 1) }` and `{ zzz(1) }` with zzz undeclared all become `Transform [ Atom:dag_token_lbrace ]`. The unprepared parse_module route (v2.compiler.staged_front_end run_front_end) dumps identically, so this is not a second lossy route beside a faithful one.",

    "EVIDENCE LEVEL, stated so the receipt is not read one rung high. The dumps ran the v2 .dag through the gunbc interpreter at main f9d37e43a1, and a structural node-count fold (not a printer) agrees: the parse tree grows with a call's arguments and nesting, while the normalized body of { g(x: 1) } is exactly one node larger than { k } -- the Transform and its lbrace atom -- and { g(x: h(y: 5)) } is no larger than that. A second named argument adds one node, so the lowering keeps something per extra argument, but none of the callee or argument content. That the natively emitted normalize behaves identically is not executed. The native route gives no contrary evidence: its receipt on the #10940 head (eager-raven-113, 2026-09-12) holds exactly one Passed identity, a literal-bodied smoke test, and every richer body refuses before or at eval (v2.compiler.inferred_tree NodeGrounding). So no route has been observed to lower a call faithfully.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder -- silent wrongness. The compiler Accepts a program with an undeclared callee and reports nothing.",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether a name is bound in the containment index is decidable, and v2 resolve already refuses an unbound VALUE name with `resolve_reason_unbound_symbol`. The missing piece is not an authority but the lowering preserving what resolve needs.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: v2 body lowering PRESERVES every call expression's callee and argument subtrees into the normalized tree on every v2 route that feeds resolve, so that resolve receives the callee as a reference. The climb's evidence is executed, and resolution alone does not discharge it. The repair that fires this trigger must show, by execution: (i) a call with a DECLARED callee executes through the native route and returns the expected ARGUMENT-DEPENDENT result, so that the argument subtree is demonstrably carried and consumed rather than merely present; (ii) a call with an UNDECLARED callee refuses at RESOLVE with a typed, located missing-binding cause -- at resolve, not later at grounding, emission or eval, since a refusal arriving downstream is consistent with the callee never having reached resolve at all; (iii) controls that discriminate ARGUMENT-subtree loss specifically, over the additional-argument and nested-call shapes named above, such that restoring the erasure makes those regression assertions FAIL rather than leaving them green. An invalid specimen that is Accepted is a FAILING must-refuse assertion, not evidence of anything. The prepared and unprepared routes and the native realization are distinct evidence paths and one passing route does not stand in for the others. A resolve-side check, a census count, or a migration of known call sites does not fire this trigger, because none of them makes the call reach resolve. These are requirements on the repair's evidence, not executions owed before this row lands.",

    "CENSUS CONSEQUENCE, recorded because the cut consumes it: the whole-tree native census (the emitted closure binary's census mode) runs only tokenize, parse and normalize per file and never calls resolve, so its roster carries front-end refusals only. Restoring call lowering does not by itself add resolve refusals to that census. That needs the census mode to resolve per module as well.",

    "CONSUMER-SIDE RECEIPT AND A SECOND SHAPE, 2026-09-13 (deep-newt-301, dispatched on `fold_shape_visible_to_no_lens`). The same route (tokenize, parse_module, normalize) was dumped for fold-family calls, which this class also erases, and for a body that is a `let` followed by a call. `{ fold(xs, init: 0, f: step) }` and `{ g(xs, init: 0, f: step) }` both become `Transform [ Atom dag_token_lbrace, Atom dag_token_int_literal, Atom step ]`: the named-argument VALUES survive as positional operands with their labels and the callee and positional `xs` dropped, which refines the earlier receipt's `a second named argument adds one node` -- what is kept is the value atom of each named argument, not the argument. The let form is a DIFFERENT erasure shape under the same class: `{ let seed = 0 \n fold(xs, init: seed, f: fn(acc, x) { .. }) }` lowers to a Bind whose body is a bare left/right sequence spine with `fold` as its leftmost atom and every right projection an empty Conj -- here the callee SURVIVES and the arguments, including an fn literal, do not, with the production shells stripped. So the two shapes lose complementary halves and neither carries a call. THE CONSUMER THIS SILENCES beyond resolve: `v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.analyze`, a required root lens at the compile door, enumerates fold sites by seam Loop or by surface fold call, and both are produced only where fold_lowering runs BEFORE this erasure -- the sole-body position. A planted quadratic after a let, in a match arm or in an if branch is Accepted with no finding, in every step spelling; enrolled RED at `gunbc.explicit_witness_admission` as `let_prefixed_fold_copy_is_caught`, `match_arm_fold_copy_is_caught` and `declared_named_step_fold_copy_is_caught` in `src/v2/test/claim/long/accumulator_copy_fold_analysis_test.dag`, each dissolving on this row's trigger. The trigger's clause (iii) gains a shape: the controls must cover the let-prefixed body, whose loss is the argument half rather than the callee half.",

    "THE ARGUMENT HALF, READ WHOLE FOR THE PLAIN SHAPES (2026-09-22, gunbc#12033), AND THE TRIGGER IS STILL NOT FIRED. Chain re-derivation of `{ step(a: x) }` -> Transform(step) found the earliest unjustified boundary one link above the operand readers: v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_call_args_from_capture received the comma list INSIDE the parens and ran body_lower_param_list_comma_spine_optional over it, a walk shaped for a capture that still carries its `(` -- on a bare comma list its skip-the-paren step skipped the FIRST ITEM, so `f(x)` kept no argument and `f(x, y)` kept y. The list is now read as the dag_grammar_comma_list_expr it is (body_lower_comma_list_items_optional, the one reader field declarations, field patterns and field initializers share) and each `arg` value goes through body_lower_value_lowered, the body walker's own entry, so `f(h(x))` carries Transform(h, x) rather than the callee atom h. Two adjacent readers were repaired on the same walk because they rebuilt an int literal without its magnitude child (body_lower_operand_ref_optional and body_lower_pattern_leaf_atom_optional's branded-atom arm), and the deep literal probe at the head of body_lower_primary_expr, which answered `f(1)`, `A(1)` and `R { v: 1 }` with the literal 1, is now shallow. MEASURED on the seed-run normalize route: `{ f(x) }` -> Transform(f, x); `{ f(x, y) }` -> Transform(f, x, y); `{ f(h(x)) }` -> Transform(f, Transform(h, x)); `{ f(1) }` -> Transform(f, 1 with magnitude); `{ A(x) }` -> Transform(A, x). WHAT IS CARRIED AND COUNTED, NOT LOWERED: a value the reader cannot lower -- a function value (`c => ..`, `fn(..) {..}`) outside a fold-family call is the named case -- is carried as its shell under the located advisory body_lowering_reason_value_carried_unlowered (v2.workflow.compile_door_cause_ownership, head grain), so the mention survives and the population is a count rather than a silence. STILL WRONG AND UNCHANGED, stated so the row is not read one rung high: a call whose argument list contains an infix (`f(x, x + 1)`) or three or more items with an operator anywhere inside is still claimed by the deep infix search of the body walker BEFORE the call arm is reached (`{ f(x, x + 1) }` -> Transform(plus, ..); `{ f(h(x), x + 1, a: 1) }` -> Transform(comma, comma, a)), the let-prefixed shape and the method-on-a-value shape are as the receipts above state, no native execution of an argument-dependent result is delivered here, and no resolve-stage refusal for an undeclared callee is claimed. The row stays open at its stated rung.",

    "PARTIAL REPAIR OF ONE SHAPE, AND THE TRIGGER IS NOT FIRED BY IT (2026-09-19, gunbc#11683, superseding gunbc#11612). A call whose CALLEE is a dotted chain -- `wall.peer.peer_leaf()`, in an expression body or a brace body -- previously lowered to the chain's FIRST ATOM with the remaining segments and the call itself dropped, so it lost both halves at once; the bare value chain `= wall.peer.peer_leaf` lost the same way even after gunbc#11582 built the spine, because the bottom-up reduce built the spine and the expression-body readers then decomposed it to its first atom, the spine not being recognised as lowered substrate. v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_dotted_chain_lowered_optional now reads both shapes off one walk (DottedChainTailRead) at the three expression sites ABOVE the first-atom fallback, and body_lower_is_core_substrate admits the spine; a call on a non-final segment (`a.f().b`) is named by the walk and declined to the existing arms (see the next sentence). Measured on the normalize route before the repair: `{ x.step(a: 1) }` reached the arrow body as `x` and `= x.field` as `x`, so the receiver-method reading and the field-access refusal of body_lower_try_postfix_projection were never reached on that route and nothing that executes is retired by lowering the bare chains and the final-segment calls to the one spine; what the head denotes is the resolver's to decide. Executed evidence: v2.test.claim.body_lowering_qualified_path, whose subject is LOWERING and whose inputs are therefore SUPPLIED AT THAT BOUNDARY (DESIGN section 3; review 68361 on gunbc#11683). Four reds that fail on main before this repair -- bare value, final-segment call, block-body call and the LOCAL-RECEIVER call -- hand parser-shaped nodes the module constructs to body_lower_dotted_chain_lowered_optional and to the expression-body and brace-body sites that consult it, beside the bare-local control that stays an atom and body_lowering_first_atom_fallback_would_truncate_the_chain, which establishes that the fallback those sites sit above answers the head atom for the same input. The DESIGN section 3 pairing is discharged by exactly two route claims that execute the real stages: body_lowering_real_parser_emits_the_supplied_dotted_shape feeds the real parser's own postfix node to the same door, and body_lowering_qualified_value_reaches_arrow_body_whole runs tokenize-parse-normalize end to end and reads the real arrow body, so deleting either integration reddens a control. A CALL ON A NON-FINAL SEGMENT (`a.f().b`, the method-on-a-value shape) IS NAMED BY THE WALK AND DECLINED, STILL ERASED: it is live idiom -- v2.workflow.floor_diff_observe floor_env_optional, v2.workflow.floor_terminal_ledger_wire ledger_wire_field_at, v2.test.claim.cargo_build_run_argv_witness, v2.lens.schedule_lens (review 68280 on gunbc#11683) -- so refusing it would have turned normalize of those modules red; it is pinned as a today-row (body_lowering_call_before_end_is_erased_today_holds, the head atom the expression-body site still answers) beside body_lowering_call_before_end_is_named_and_declined, which reads the DECLINED verdict by name so a reader that simply stopped recognising the shape cannot satisfy the row. THE ARGUMENT HALF, MEASURED ON THE SAME ROUTE AND UNTOUCHED: a plain `{ step(a: x) }` reaches the arrow body as Transform(step) with the named argument dropped, `{ step(x, 1) }` as the bare literal `1`, and `{ x.step(a: 1) }` after this change as Transform(spine x.step) with no argument -- the callee half is repaired for the dotted shapes and the argument half stays as this row states it. WHAT THIS DOES NOT DISCHARGE, stated so the row is not read one rung high: this row's trigger names the whole call-expression population and demands argument-dependent NATIVE execution, a resolve-stage refusal for an undeclared callee, and controls that discriminate ARGUMENT-subtree loss. None of those is delivered here, the argument subtrees of other call shapes are untouched, and the row stays open at its stated rung.",
    "THE MID-CHAIN CALL IS NO LONGER ERASED, AND THE ROW STAYS OPEN (2026-09-22, gunbc#12033's PR2). The previous receipt records that a call on a NON-FINAL segment -- `a.f().b`, the method-on-a-value shape -- was NAMED by the walk and DECLINED to the pre-existing arms, where it stayed erased to the head atom with no diagnostic, and that the decline was chosen because refusing it would have reddened normalize of the four live sites (v2.workflow.floor_diff_observe floor_env_optional, v2.workflow.floor_terminal_ledger_wire ledger_wire_field_at, v2.test.claim.cargo_build_run_argv_witness, v2.lens.schedule_lens). The DERIVATION that receipt did not carry, and which this one does: the arms it declined to read exactly ONE repeat element of the postfix chain and then decided, so the erasure was not specific to the mid-chain call at all -- it was a single-step reader standing where a fold over the step sequence belongs, and the same boundary produced BOTH a silent drop (`fields.skip(n: i).first()` built Transform(skip, fields, i) and dropped `.first()`) and a located refusal (`shell.Env.Get(name: n).value` refused postfix_field_access_refused off its first step `.Env`). v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold now reads the whole step sequence in one walk (PostfixChainRead) and folds it left-associatively (body_lower_postfix_chain_fold_step): the spine accumulates bare segments, the first call suffix closes it into a Transform through that path, and every step after it is an elimination of a VALUE -- a method call, or a field projection (v2.std.node_query field_projection_node). body_lower_try_postfix_projection and its unowned cause postfix_field_access_refused are DELETED; the residue that genuinely is not lowered -- a step suffix that is neither empty nor a parenthesised argument row, which today means the module-qualified record construction `a.b.C { f: v }` and an `as` suffix -- DECLINES to the pre-existing arms under a counted head-grain advisory; what it does NOT do is refuse, and the single present-tense authority for its behaviour is body_lowering_reason_postfix_suffix_carried, stated below. AN EARLIER REVISION OF THIS CHANGE MADE IT REFUSE INSTEAD, under a cause that never landed and exists nowhere in the corpus, AND THE MEASUREMENT IS WHY IT WAS WITHDRAWN: refusing the unlowered suffix kinds turned 32 modules that ACCEPT at base into refusals -- 28 directly under that withdrawn cause and 4 more as match_arm_navigation_refused, where the rejection propagated out of a match scrutinee. That is the same trade #11683 faced for the call-before-end class and resolved the same way, so the brace suffix (`a.b.C { f: v }`) and the `as` suffix DECLINE to the pre-existing arms and keep behaving exactly as they do on base. Their erasure therefore REMAINS, is not claimed repaired by this change, and stays a today-row on this class; lowering them needs a construct tag able to carry a qualified name, which is a wider package. The cause row was removed with the refusal rather than left rostered with no producer. WHAT THAT FIRST WITHDRAWAL GOT WRONG, AND WHAT REVIEW 70078 CAUGHT: declining them SILENTLY would have moved the class from mitigatable to BELOW the ladder, because on base these shapes reached a LOUD located refusal (the deleted postfix_field_access_refused) and DESIGN section 4b forbids silent wrongness outright rather than admitting it as a declared drop. The measurement behind the withdrawal only ran in the base-accepts-to-head-refuses direction (32 modules); the converse direction is 8 of the 42 base-refusing files carrying a brace suffix, so the population is real. The door therefore declines AND emits body_lowering_reason_postfix_suffix_carried at HEAD grain (rostered in v2.workflow.compile_door_cause_ownership), the same shape gunbc#12033 used for value_carried_unlowered: the file still Accepts so nothing that accepts on base regresses, and the residue stays located and countable instead of vanishing. EXECUTED EVIDENCE, and it is a discriminating red rather than a demonstration that the new fold works: v2.test.claim.body_lowering_qualified_path body_lowering_call_before_end_keeps_every_step is the row that PREVIOUSLY asserted the erasure (as body_lowering_call_before_end_is_erased_today_holds, kept expressly so it would flip the day the shape was lowered or refused). It now asserts the whole chain survives as a field projection off the call, it is RED against the pre-repair fold because the pre-repair answer is the bare atom `a`, and per DESIGN section 4b(4) it stays enrolled as the regression control now that it greens; body_lowering_call_before_end_is_not_the_head_atom is its negative half and body_lowering_call_before_end_is_found_as_two_steps reads the walk's own verdict so a reader that merely stopped recognising the shape cannot satisfy the set. WHAT STAYS OPEN, so the row is not read one rung high: this row's trigger names the WHOLE call-expression population and demands argument-dependent native execution, a resolve-stage refusal for an undeclared callee, and controls that discriminate ARGUMENT-subtree loss. None of that is delivered here. Infix inside an argument list is still claimed by the deep infix search, a function value outside a fold call is still CARRIED as its shell under body_lowering_reason_value_carried_unlowered, and the postfix chain is one call shape among several.",

    "THE ARGUMENT HALF, REPAIRED, AND A CORRECTION TO THIS ROW'S OWN PREMISE (2026-09-23, gunbc#12108, merge b0d307c31b, measured_at b8e0cc4eb9). The premise elsewhere in the XL-2 program that call arguments were represented after lowering was FALSE, and this row's earlier reading that named-argument VALUES survive as positional operands does not hold for plain calls on the production normalize route: v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_call_args_from_capture asked the PARAMETER-list spine reader for a comma spine, that reader answered Present on the first argument's inner sequence because an argument capture arrives with its parentheses already consumed, and the collector beneath it found nothing -- so every argument of a plain call, named or positional, lowered to a call with ZERO arguments, and the fact was absent from the normalized tree rather than lost between the tree and the denominator. The repair is a structural, fail-closed reader of the grammar's own comma-list shape that refuses any position it cannot read. Executed: v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_mention_survival a_call_argument_mention_is_reachable_by_the_collector_holds and its positional and tree-grain rows, and v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.call_argument_resolve_refusal, whose undeclared named and positional argument rows refuse at resolve located at the argument and FAIL on b8e0cc4eb9. This discharges clause (ii)'s argument analogue and clause (iii) for plain calls; it does NOT fire this row's trigger, which still names argument-dependent NATIVE execution over the whole call population; the mid-chain call (a.f().b) is the preceding receipt's. The XL-2 carrier records this as gunbc.compiler_frontend_program_status Xl2Prerequisite PlainCallArgumentReferenceVisibility.",

    "THE CALL-THEN-FIELD RESIDUE, AND A SILENT TRUNCATION FOUND ON THE WAY (2026-09-25, MQ-1, fierce-boar-95). warm-bear-132's chunk c02590 (v2.compiler.parse parse_memo_recurrence_census: `acc + expr_parse_demand_fold(expr: p.expression).discarding_sites`) refused operator_operand_unread once gunbc#12210 lowered the enclosing fn literal. Re-deriving the slice found TWO boundaries. (1) The chain door v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_postfix_chain_lowered_from_steps could lower a head that was a bare segment or an operand reference, but not a RAW call: on the top-down walker route the head `f(x)` is still a primary carrying its call suffix, so the door declined and the operand refused. The head is now lowered by the walker's own call reader (body_lower_try_primary_ident_call), and every step after it folds as it does off any value. (2) Worse and silent: the projection the chain fold produces (v2.std.node_query field_projection_node) was not recognised by body_lower_is_core_substrate, so on the bottom-up route every reader above the postfix reduce -- an operator operand, a paren group, a unary operand -- re-read it as unlowered and descended to its BASE: `p + g(x).a` lowered to `p + g(x)` with no diagnostic, while a match scrutinee (read through body_lower_value_lowered) kept it. The predicate now admits the projection through field_projection_optional, the construct arm's reason. (3) Reference conservation then refused the projected field as a dropped reference: field_projection_node stamped the field atom with the WHOLE chain's occurrence, so the authored segment's minted occurrence was in no lowered node. Each PostfixStep now carries the segment's authored node (PostfixStep.at) and the projection is stamped from it. Controls: v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.value_position_whole_read a_field_projection_on_a_call_result_in_an_operand_lowers_whole and a_two_step_projection_on_a_call_result_lowers_every_step, and v2.test.claim.namespace_xl0.reference_conservation_admission a_field_projection_on_a_call_result_in_an_operand_is_admitted_holds; removing either change reds them (measured). STILL OPEN, and not this shape: a `let` value that is a call lowers to the callee's first atom (`let x = g(e: p)` keeps only `g`), with or without a projection -- the let slice's, not the chain door's.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
